 "summary": "Fixes Include-What-You-Use (IWYU) warnings across fuzz tests and test utilities in `src/test/fuzz`, and configures CI to treat any future IWYU warnings in these directories as errors. It separates the `NodeId` declaration into a dedicated `node/node_id.h` header to resolve symbol ambiguity for tooling, updates related headers in `net` and `node/eviction`, and adds a lint check enforcing that all code in headers is inside include guards.",
 "problem": "Fuzz tests rely on transitive header inclusions, leaving include lists incomplete and causing IWYU static analysis in CI to fail or remain unenforced for `src/test/fuzz`. Furthermore, duplicate declarations of types like `NodeId` make header ownership ambiguous for static analysis tools.",
 "evidence": [
  "PR description: 'This PR continues the ongoing effort to enforce IWYU warnings. See Developer Notes.'",
  "Commit 86296b1bf6: 'Two identical declarations of NodeId make it ambiguous for static tools such as IWYU which header should provide the symbol.'"
 ],
